WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.595
Cameras are common payloads for still imagery and video.

00:00:03.595 --> 00:00:07.479
Mission requirements determine resolution, field of view, stabilization, frame rate,

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:08.644
and capture interval.

00:00:08.644 --> 00:00:12.916
Higher settings increase storage and processing without automatically improving the decision.

00:00:12.916 --> 00:00:19.130
Thermal sensors measure emitted energy and can support inspection or search tasks at a high level,

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.625
but interpretation depends on calibration, environment, surface properties, distance,

00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:23.790
and operator competence.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:28.839
A thermal image does not directly measure every condition a viewer may infer.

00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:34.276
Mapping payloads and software combine overlapping observations into products such as orthomosaics or models.

00:00:34.276 --> 00:00:37.771
Useful mapping requires appropriate overlap, consistent coverage, position quality,

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:38.936
and documented processing.

00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:42.043
The final product should state accuracy and limitations.

00:00:42.043 --> 00:00:45.927
Metadata may include time, position, altitude estimate, device, camera settings,

00:00:45.927 --> 00:00:47.092
and software history.

00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:52.141
It supports organization and analysis but may also expose sensitive locations or operations.

00:00:52.141 --> 00:00:54.471
Preserve needed metadata while controlling distribution.

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:58.355
Match the payload and collection pattern to the mission purpose.

00:00:58.355 --> 00:01:00.296
Collecting extra views, private areas,

00:01:00.296 --> 00:01:04.568
or unrelated people creates privacy and storage risk without adding value.

00:01:04.568 --> 00:01:08.840
Plan camera direction, flight path, and retention to minimize unnecessary capture.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.501
Assess data quality during the mission when safe, then verify after landing.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:17.384
Protect media during offload, label it to the flight record,

00:01:17.384 --> 00:01:19.326
and preserve originals when required.

00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:25.540
Data is part of the operation and deserves the same planning and accountability as the aircraft.
